## Why This Is Asked

Tests for idempotent APIs are critical in distributed systems to prevent duplicate side effects, especially with downstream payment and warehouse services.

## Key Concepts

- Idempotency keys and deduplication
- Retry semantics and backoff strategies
- End-to-end vs component-level contracts
- Data isolation across clients

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example Express snippet demonstrating idempotency handling
const orders = new Map();
app.post('/orders', async (req, res) => {
  const key = req.headers['idempotency-key'];
  if (!key) return res.status(400).send({error:'Idempotency-Key required'});
  if (orders.has(key)) return res.json({ orderId: orders.get(key).orderId, cached:true });
  const orderId = generateOrderId();
  // simulate payment call etc.
  orders.set(key, { orderId });
  res.json({ orderId });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test that a retry after a 5xx does not generate a new order with a different id?
- How would you structure tests to verify idempotency across multiple services (gateway, payment, warehouse)?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical end-to-end reliability under high concurrency, including idempotency, external dependencies, and reconciliation. 

## Key Concepts
- Idempotency keys, Redis-backed deduplication
- Asynchronous queues, external bank API faults, retries
- Webhook delivery guarantees and replay protection
- Ledger reconciliation and observability

## Code Example
```javascript
const request = require('supertest');
const app = require('../src/app');

test('idempotent payments with same key yields single ledger write', async () => {
  const key = 'abc123';
  const payload = { amount: 100, currency: 'USD', merchant: 'ACME' };
  const t1 = request(app).post('/payments').set('Idempotency-Key', key).send(payload);
  const t2 = request(app).post('/payments').set('Idempotency-Key', key).send(payload);
  const [r1, r2] = await Promise.all([t1, t2]);
  expect(r1.status).toBe(200);
  expect(r2.status).toBe(200);
  // verify a single ledger entry created via test hooks or API mocks
});
```

